{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"tl-v1","tool":"ragflow_retrieval","arguments":{"dataset_ids":["918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37"],"question":"CMT-2026-09-004 Singapore 180ms RTT 5s prototype timeout 30s high-latency links zero-trust node sync handshake","page_size":10,"vector_similarity_weight":0.3,"similarity_threshold":0.2,"top_k":1024,"keyword":false,"metadata_condition":{"logic":"and","conditions":[{"name":"path","comparison_operator":"is","value":"sources"}]}},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"chunks\": [{\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-26\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Node Sync Handshake Prototype\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-06\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 09:30] Bob**: Starting on the replication handshake for the zero-trust node sync. First requirement is that two nodes have to authenticate each other before either one accepts replicated entries.\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 09:37] Evan**: How's a node proving who it is right now?\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 09:38] Bob**: Each node has a registered identity it presents at connect time. If the peer doesn't recognize it, the connection gets dropped before any data moves.\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 09:49] Charlie**: Does the handshake add noticeable overhead to the redaction jobs running on the same box?\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 10:40] Bob**: Negligible so far — it's a short exchange before the sync session opens, nothing that touches the active redaction path.\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 10:41] Diana**: What's next after the prototype?\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 11:47] Bob**: Need to check it holds up under real network delay, not just on my two test nodes on the same switch. That's the next pass.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 26 slack thread node sync handshak prototyp channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 06 2026 08 06 09 30 bob start on the replic handshak for the zero trust node sync first requir is that two node have to authent each other befor either one accept replic entri 2026 08 06 09 37 evan how s a node prove who it is right now 2026 08 06 09 38 bob each node ha a regist ident it present at connect time if the peer doesn t recogn it the connect get drop befor ani data move 2026 08 06 09 49 charli doe the handshak add notic overhead to the redact job run on the same box 2026 08 06 10 40 bob neglig so far it s a short exchang befor the sync session open noth that touch the activ redact path 2026 08 06 10 41 diana what s next after the prototyp 2026 08 06 11 47 bob need to check it hold up under real network delay not just on my two test node on the same switch that s the next pas\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ede2c2fa8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-06-node-sync-handshake-prototype.md\", \"id\": \"4bd5b5740e6d4a32\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.35764964126146864, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1676997432306695, \"vector_similarity\": 0.80086607, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-06-node-sync-handshake-prototype.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ede2c2fa8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-06-node-sync-handshake-prototype.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-06-node-sync-handshake-prototype.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1079, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:08:46\", \"token_count\": 317, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-27\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Node Sync Handshake Validation\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-08-08\\n\